262 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 204 0 R/E(Animal HealthCare Center \(AHCC\) is a locally owned veterinary clinic located in Wellington, Florida. It offers a full range of services, including wellness exams, vaccinations, dental cleanings, surgeries, diagnostics, acupuncture, and boarding. For nearly three decades, AHCC has taken pride in providing compassionate, comprehensive, and high-quality care for every pet that walks through the door. )/Pg 12 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

263 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 204 0 R/E(With a loyal clientele primarily composed of women between the ages of 45 and 65 \(Meta, n.d.\), they view their pets as family members. AHCC has built its reputation through providing exceptional medical care, creating genuine relationships, and creating a warm and welcoming environment for both pets and clients alike.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

264 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 204 0 R/E(Pet ownership in the United States is continuing to rise. According to data from the American Pet Products Association, \215pet ownership in the U.S. hit an estimated 94 million households in 2025, up from 82 million in 2023\216 \(IBPSA, 2025\). The same report goes into specifics, stating that \215U.S. households reported ownership of approximately 68 million dogs, up from 65.1 million in the 2023-2024 survey, and that cat ownership also rose, from 46.5 million to 49 million over the same period\216 \(Wall, 2025\). This steady increase highlights the need for finding trustworthy veterinary care. To address this growing demand, AHCC has developed the Sit, Stay, Be Healthy social media campaign. )/Pg 12 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

265 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 204 0 R/E(This campaign, running from January to March, aims to build on AHCC\220s reputation as a trusted, full-service clinic while encouraging pet owners to take an active role in their pets' health. The campaign's primary goal is to educate and inspire clients to prioritize their pets' care and regular health checkups, ensuring they live long and healthy lives. )/Pg 12 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

266 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 204 0 R/E(The Sit, Stay, Be Healthy campaign will focus on proactive pet care while highlighting AHCC\220s range of services. Over the three months, each month will spotlight two of the clinic's services centered around seasonal themes and national awareness months. The campaign will specifically focus on wellness exams, vaccinations, dental cleanings, surgical procedures, preventive care, and acupuncture. )/Pg 12 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

267 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 204 0 R/E(This campaign will utilize a strategic blend of educational content, client testimonials, and other engaging visuals to enhance AHCC\220s online presence and foster stronger relationships with its audience members. Both paid and organic advertisements will be used, with a greater emphasis on paid strategies to increase brand awareness, audience engagement, PetDesk app downloads, and appointment bookings, specifically through online booking on the PetDesk app or its website. )/Pg 12 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

268 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 204 0 R/E(Overall, the goal of the Sit, Stay, Be Healthy campaign reflects AHCC\220s commitment to providing compassionate and comprehensive care to all pets that come to the clinic. By focusing on the content outlined, it positions AHCC as a trusted provider in every pet's life, allowing them to \215sit, stay, and be healthy\216 for years to come. )/Pg 12 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

269 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 204 0 R/E(3)/Pg 12 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

270 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 205 0 R/E(Loyal client base: Animal HealthCare Center has established a strong and loyal client base over the past 28 years. Some clients even followed the lead veterinarian from his previous practice, 43 miles away. This demonstrates not only the clinic's services but also a deep trust in the consistent quality of care delivered by our veterinary staff. On social media, this translates to repeat bookings through link clicks, likes, comments, and shares. )/Pg 13 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

271 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 205 0 R/E(Office Cat \215Mascots\216: AHCC has two cats, Bravo and Lainey, who live in the office and are loved by clients. These cats are frequently featured in the clinic\220s social media content, and posts that include them typically receive higher engagement compared to other formats. By showcasing the cats, AHCC not only humanizes the brand but also creates authentic, shareable content that strengthens emotional connection with clients.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

272 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 205 0 R/E(Heavy reliance on organic growth: AHCC rarely uses paid advertising, and when it does, the implementation is inconsistent. Instead, it heavily relies on organic material for growth and visibility, slowing things down dramatically. According to Baurai \(2024\), \215paid ads amplify reach, allow for targeted advertising and provide measurable ROI,\216 all of which AHCC is missing out on when not committing to a structured paid ad strategy. )/Pg 13 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

273 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 205 0 R/E(Content Format Limitations: AHCC social media posts primarily consist of static images and graphics, with a few animated ones occasionally included. While content usually is consistent, it does not perform as strongly as video or interactive content. "Static ads are far less effective than video. Video ads usually have a 25% higher impression rate than static ads. They also drive more social media engagement" \(QuickFrame, 2022\). Its over-reliance on static content limits AHCC's ability to maximize its social media potential.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

274 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 205 0 R/T(SWOT Analysis)/E(SWOT Analysis)/Pg 13 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

