279 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 206 0 R/E(Integrate more short-form video content: AHCC can strengthen its social media presence by posting more short-form video content, such as Instagram and Facebook reels. Both Instagram and Facebook tend to prioritize video content in their algorithms, making it easier to reach new audiences beyond the current client base. It can also be beneficial to integrate them with videos promoting its services that include booking links, as QuickFrame \(2022\) notes, "When looking at Clicks, marketers found that videos drove almost 30% more clicks than simply static image assets.")/Pg 14 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

280 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 206 0 R/E(Invest in more paid advertising: As mentioned previously, AHCC primarily focuses on organic growth, which greatly limits visibility outside of its established client base. By investing in consistent paid advertising on Facebook and Instagram, AHCC can reach areas beyond the Wellington/Lake Worth region. Paid ads also enable AHCC to target specific demographics, ensuring that the messaging reaches the intended audience. The investment doesn't need to be large, especially for a single hospital clinic. Even a very modest budget can generate meaningful results. )/Pg 14 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

281 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 206 0 R/E(Rising economic costs: According to the American Veterinary Medical Association \(2025\), \215The rising financial anxiety comes amid an upward trend in lifetime pet care costs since 2022: 11.7% for dogs and 19.4% for cats. The report says these increases can be attributed to both higher prices, as well as pet owners\220 growing commitment to invest in their pets\220 health and care.\216 When clients are in challenging financial situations, pet owners may delay veterinary care or opt for lower-cost providers. )/Pg 14 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

282 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 206 0 R/E(Increased Local Competition: The Wellington area has several locally owned and corporately owned veterinary hospitals. While AHCC has a loyal client base, increased competition can sometimes make it harder to attract new clients. Some of these practices can heavily lean on promotions or memberships to get people through the door. The increased saturation means that AHCC must work harder to differentiate itself in terms of trust and quality of care, thereby reducing the risk of losing potential clients to competitors. )/Pg 14 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

