288 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 207 0 R/E(Animal HealthCare Center \(AHCC\) is a full-service veterinary clinic located in Wellington, Florida. The clinic has a strong, loyal audience base, primarily composed of women aged between 45 and 65 \(Meta, n.d.\), who are long-time clients and often treat their pets as family members. This audience is far more active on Facebook than on Instagram, which is consistent with research that states that adults aged 30\20549 report 78% usage of Facebook compared to 66% usage of Instagram, while adults aged 50\20564 show 70% usage of Facebook compared to just 36% for Instagram \(Sprout Social, 2024\). Furthermore, BrightLocal \(2022\) states that adults aged 30-60 rely heavily on Google reviews when evaluating local businesses, making online reputation especially important for AHCC\220s loyal base. They are particularly responsive to community-driven posts such as Testimonial Tuesday, often sharing their experiences in the comments of those posts, as well as engaging with content featuring the office cats Bravo and Lainey.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

289 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 207 0 R/E(Though this group remains important to AHCC and plays a crucial part in their success, the target audience for this campaign will be slightly younger. For the Sit, Stay, Be Healthy, AHCC will target older Gen Z and younger Millennials between the ages of 20 and 35 in Wellington and the surrounding areas. This audience is likely to include first-time pet owners, young students, professionals, and young families. We should target this audience because it enables AHCC to expand its reach, increase awareness of its services, and drive more appointment bookings through online booking, while still nurturing its loyal and established base of 45-64-year-olds.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

