endobj

439 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 217 0 R/E(AHCC can introduce interactive client engagement initiatives. This allows for a two-way conversation between the clinic and the clients. For example, the clinic will create polls, fact or myth games, and pet tips on its social media pages to engage its audiences. This allows for a two-way conversation between the clinic and the clients. Two-way conversations allow businesses to \215interact with customers in real time through messaging apps, SMS, and social platforms. This responsive communication builds trust, improves customer satisfaction, and creates opportunities for personalized engagement, ultimately driving loyalty and sales\216 \(St. Pierre, 2025\). This helps support goals two and three by strengthening existing client relationships through participation and increasing overall engagement across Facebook and Instagram.)/Pg 25 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

440 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 217 0 R/E(AHCC can incorporate user-generated-content \(UGC\) and testimonials from clients more across Instagram and Facebook. According to MacNaught \(2024\), \215Testimonials and reviews are powerful forms of user-generated content. They add authenticity, build trust and social proof, and enhance a brand\220s reputation. Testimonials can increase conversions by 34%, and 66% of consumers consider positive user reviews the most important factor when making purchasing decisions.\216 These posts will highlight recent feedback that it has received on Google or through direct feedback through Birdeye, its reputation and review management system. This strategy supports goals one, two, and three: it increases brand awareness by showcasing real stories of its services, and it strengthens existing relationships. It builds trust through proof of high-quality care, and it increases engagement by encouraging other clients to share content and interact with AHCC.)/Pg 25 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

