endobj

480 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 221 0 R/E(This image will be the cover for a carousel post that will be featured on Instagram. It will feature one of AHCC's veterinarians' answers to the top misconceptions about pet prevention. This type of content reinforces AHCC's goals by promoting educational and engaging content that encourages clients to take a proactive approach to their pets' health. By featuring one of its veterinarians, the clinic helps build trust and credibility, positioning itself as the go-to animal hospital in the community.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

481 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 221 0 R/E(This post closely connects with January's "healthy start" theme, as it encourages clients to begin the new year by prioritizing their pets' health. By sharing their wellness tips, clients can inspire each other to prioritize their pets' health. This post thereby promotes community engagement, increases audience interaction, and reinforces the overall theme of the Sit, Stay, Be Healthy campaign by highlighting the importance of proactive pet care.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

482 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 221 0 R/E(20)/Pg 29 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

483 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 222 0 R/T(Proposed )/E(Proposed )/Pg 30 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

484 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 222 0 R/T(Timeline)/E(Timeline)/Pg 30 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

485 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 222 0 R/E(January will focus on wellness exams and vaccinations. These go hand in hand as vaccines are often given during the pet's wellness exams. During this month, the clinic will emphasize the importance of annual exams and keeping pets up to date on their vaccines as part of a health and preventative care routine. The content will include educational materials and videos about each topic, as well as highlight the PetDesk app, which sends out automatic reminders for wellness exams and vaccinations. It also allows clients to have their pets' medical records right on their phone and provides an easy way to schedule appointments.)/Pg 30 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

486 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 222 0 R/T(February)/E(February)/Pg 30 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

487 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 222 0 R/E(February will focus on dental cleaning and surgical procedures. Because February is both National Pet Dental Health Month and National Spay/Neuter Awareness Month, this timing aligns perfectly with this campaign's offerings. Dental posts will include before-and-after images and educational facts about oral health. They will also mention the 10% discount we offer to clients whose pets are recommended for dental procedures and who book within the next month. Surgical content will emphasize AHCC's surgical capabilities, including mass removals, soft tissue surgeries, and more, with a special focus on spays and neuters due to the month's theme. Posts will focus on educating clients about responsible pet ownership and the importance of spaying and neutering their pets. They will also spotlight the clinic's commitment to safety, using the highest quality surgical equipment and providing excellent postoperative care. )/Pg 30 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

488 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 222 0 R/T(January)/E(January)/Pg 30 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

489 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 222 0 R/T(The Animal HealthCare Center\220s \215Sit, Stay, Be Healthy\216 campaign will launch on January 1st, 2026, and run through March 31st, 2026. The campaign will begin at the start of the year because, according to Faraci \(2024\), \215January gives us a clean slate and can make us more optimistic about its ability to change and more motivated to take action.\216 This three-month campaign allows Animal HealthCare Center \(AHCC\) to build strong awareness around the clinic\220s preventative and specialized services. Each month in the campaign will feature two services that AHCC offers to educate clients and strengthen awareness of its full range of care. )/E(The Animal HealthCare Center\220s \215Sit, Stay, Be Healthy\216 campaign will launch on January 1st, 2026, and run through March 31st, 2026. The campaign will begin at the start of the year because, according to Faraci \(2024\), \215January gives us a clean slate and can make us more optimistic about its ability to change and more motivated to take action.\216 This three-month campaign allows Animal HealthCare Center \(AHCC\) to build strong awareness around the clinic\220s preventative and specialized services. Each month in the campaign will feature two services that AHCC offers to educate clients and strengthen awareness of its full range of care. )/Pg 30 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

490 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 222 0 R/E(March will focus on parasite prevention and acupuncture. This timing also aligns well with the timing of this campaign, as \215spring marks the beginning of peak season for fleas, ticks, intestinal worms, and other parasites that can affect both pets and livestock\216 \(Clinic, n.d.\). Posts will be largely educational, focusing on prevention products like Heartgard and NexGard, and will remind clients about the importance of parasite prevention. Acupuncture will also be a focus in March, as it is a brand-new service we are starting to offer in 2026. Content will include information on acupuncture and its benefits, while also emphasizing AHCC\220s commitment to pets' wellbeing by adding new services.)/Pg 30 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

491 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 222 0 R/T(March)/E(March)/Pg 30 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

492 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 222 0 R/T(One major pro to this campaign is that it aligns with monthly awareness themes that naturally support AHCC's services. January capitalizes on the new year motivation and aligns with the idea of starting the year off on a healthy foot. February ties into two national month themes: National Pet Dental Health Month and Spay/Neuter Awareness Month, allowing AHCC to promote both dental and surgical procedures strongly. March also ties into a monthly theme with World Parasite Day on March 20th. One potential con to this campaign is that promoting two services in one month could make it difficult to promote each service equally and fully address the campaign's goals.)/E(One major pro to this campaign is that it aligns with monthly awareness themes that naturally support AHCC's services. January capitalizes on the new year motivation and aligns with the idea of starting the year off on a healthy foot. February ties into two national month themes: National Pet Dental Health Month and Spay/Neuter Awareness Month, allowing AHCC to promote both dental and surgical procedures strongly. March also ties into a monthly theme with World Parasite Day on March 20th. One potential con to this campaign is that promoting two services in one month could make it difficult to promote each service equally and fully address the campaign's goals.)/Pg 30 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

