endobj

502 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 223 0 R/E(The Sit, Stay, Be Healthy campaign will use two methods to measure ROI: Return on Ad Spend \(ROAS\) and Standard Financial ROI. ROAS will assess the effectiveness of the overall ad spend from paid social media advertising in generating revenue for AHCC. Using Meta Business Suite's Ads Manager for Facebook and Instagram. Approximately 31% of the total budget is allocated towards paid media advertising for its services. Therefore, it is essential to determine whether these investments are translating into client actions, such as appointment bookings, whether the client books online or by calling the office. We can consider this a success if the revenue generated from the ads exceeds the total amount spent on paid advertising, as it indicates that the campaign encouraged pet owners to take their pets' health seriously. Standard Financial ROI will also be used to measure the success of this campaign. This method measures revenue against spend to determine if the campaign generated a positive financial return for AHCC. Unlike ROAS, ROI evaluates the profitability of the campaign as a whole, including all costs and revenue earned, as opposed to tracking paid advertising only. This will enable AHCC to determine whether the campaign was financially successful and assess the effectiveness of the marketing efforts in contributing to the clinic's growth. )/Pg 31 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

503 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 223 0 R/E(Social media metrics are data points that track the performance and influence of a company\220s social channels, content, and strategy \(Hill, 2025\). The metrics that will be used to evaluate this campaign are appointment growth rate and cost per conversion. The appointment growth rate will be calculated after the campaign\220s three-month duration and compared to the same frame as last year. This metric will help AHCC determine the success of the campaign in attracting both new and existing clients to book services, such as wellness exams, dental cleanings, and acupuncture. Cost per conversion is another important metric that AHCC will be measuring in this campaign.\216Cost per conversion is a metric that calculates the cost of getting one new customer or turning a lead into an actual sale and can be done during any marketing campaign to help gauge its effectiveness and determine how much a business has gained or lost\216 \(Dataflo, n.d.\). For AHCC specifically, it will help determine the effectiveness of its paid media on Facebook and Instagram in converting engagement into appointment bookings. )/Pg 31 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

504 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 223 0 R/T(Metrics)/E(Metrics)/Pg 31 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

